WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.100
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.200
Thank you for being here.
I appreciate this.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.501
When you guys
started this -- in 1984?

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.534
-[ Laughs ] Yes.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.100
-We don't remember.
We think so.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.701
-Did you see yourselves
being together in 2022 in '84?

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.868
Or you don't think that far --
-40 years later?

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.601
No, I am pretty sure -- Like --
I'm pretty sure the only reason

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.167
we're still together
40 years later

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:25.701
is because suicide pacts
apparently are not binding.

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:28.868
-Wow!
-That, and we're Canadian.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.734
It's too impolite to break up.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:33.467
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-It makes a lot of noise.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.133
-That's why the divorce rate
in Canada is zero.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.267
-No, it doesn't --
Everyone's too polite.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.200
Here's you guys here.
Look at these.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.801
-Ah.
-Aww.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.234
-Look how cute we are.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:46.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.033
-Oh, you just want throw us
over your shoulder and burp us.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.734
-Really just want
to burp you guys.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.968
I've obviously loved you.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:56.367
But I think I know you, but you
guys didn't even start together.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.901
Is that correct? You were
different sketch groups?

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:00.501
-Yes, we were two different
sketch groups.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:02.634
We were The Audience...
-From Calgary!

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:06.000
-...which was Mark's name.
A lot of Calgarians here.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.634
-We were the Kids in the Hall
in Toronto.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.200
-Yep.
-Whoo!

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.634
-And --
-Some guy.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.634
-And some guy.
-I was an actor.

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.868
-Oh, of course!
-I was a real actor.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.434
-Exactly, Scott, yes.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:19.667
And how did you all
end up coming together

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.100
and forming the band?

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.501
-Scott booted his way in.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.167
-Well, they'd all been together.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.300
And I saw them one night
in a midnight show.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.000
And my friend Darlene
dragged me down.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.501
And we were in an audience.
There was about seven people.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.367
And they weren't doing
that well.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:35.133
And there wasn't really anybody
in the audience

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.267
to let them know
how badly they were doing,

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.267
but I fell in love with them
right away.

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.667
And I thought to myself,
"I need to be in that group."

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.801
And I noticed
underneath the chair,

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:47.200
there was a doughnut taped --
-From a really bad scene idea.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.267
-Then I found some other
doughnuts taped in other seats.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:53.567
And I went, "Oh, I bet those
doughnuts are part of a bit.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:56.300
Maybe I should ruin the bit.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:01.033
And then they'll see me."
And you want to be seen.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.100
-Of course!
-So I grab the doughnuts

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.534
and I just started whipping it
at them on stage.

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:09.734
And I remember Bruce going,
"What the [bleep]...?"

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:12.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:16.434
I go like,
"It's me! I'm here!"

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:17.467
-"Your new friend!"

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.234
-I just wanted them
to notice me.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:22.133
And it could have gone
a lot worse though.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.834
-It went pretty bad.
-It was bad, but --

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.534
This part,
they don't even know, really.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:29.601
Buy I had a cross bow
with me, as well. People --

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:31.000
-It could have been much worse.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.868
-Well, I just came
from a Renn fair.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.133
I was going to fire bolts
just above their heads,

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.701
so, luckily,
I went for the doughnuts.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.367
-Doughnuts.
Always go for the doughnuts.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:39.801
-Thank you.
-And now here we are.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:42.868
-And did -- did you
all get discovered by Lorne?

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.501
Like, how did that --
'Cause I know

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:45.968
I auditioned for Lorne Michaels.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.133
But did he -- did he find you?

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.667
Or did he -- how did that work?

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.534
-Well, he actually sent people
to Toronto

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:54.367
when we were doing a show,
and it was the week we got

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:57.133
a really rave review
in "The Globe and Mail,"

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.968
which is a newspaper
up in Canada.

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:01.534
And so we're actually
at the theater

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.033
rehearsing after
this rave review

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.834
and I'm probably reading it
over and over.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:06.267
And then the phone rang,

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.968
and it was the talent bookers
from "Saturday Night Live."

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.300
They said, "Oh, we read
about your show.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.934
We want to come." And I said,
"Well, it's sold out."

00:03:12.934 --> 00:03:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.834
And then I said, "Well, maybe
we'll do a run in a year or so."

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:20.100
And I said, "Well, you're
from 'Saturday Night Live.'

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.400
You got a lot of money.
You can scalp tickets perhaps."

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.234
And then I hung up the phone.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.133
And I looked over
at my four friends here

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.501
and realized
I did a wrong thing.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.767
So I called the nice lady back,
and here we are, yeah.

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:33.367
-Yeah, and then he saw you
and said,

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:34.667
"Oh, yeah, you guys are great"?

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.701
-Yeah, we had Lorne --
Eventually,

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:40.300
Lorne came up and saw one
of our shows in Toronto.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.501
And you know -- you know Lorne.
Lorne's a laugher.

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:46.501
He's so easy to make laugh.
And Lorne has a beautiful laugh.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.334
-Did he -- Did he laugh?
-Oh, he laughed.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.000
Lorne has like -- He laughs
like an old-timey cowboy.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.367
Like the chuck-wagon cook.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.701
All they way through the --
he was just going --

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:59.467
[ Wheezing laughter ]

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.067
"By gum!"

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:03.467
Yeah, the whole crowd
was staring at him.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.534
No one really paid attention
to us at all.

00:04:05.534 --> 00:04:07.200
-So he didn't laugh at all?
-No.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.267
-He didn't laugh at all.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.567
-He looked bemused
several times.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.200
-At least he stayed
for the whole thing.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.734
-Yeah, he did stay --
Well, not the whole thing.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.501
I think --
-No.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.033
We did like a 3-hour show.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.367
-We did like a 3-1/2-hour show.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.100
-And then, afterwards,
at the half, I went up to him

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.400
and said,
"And now, Lorne, guess what.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.534
After the break,
we're gonna do some improv.

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:26.801
Do you want to stick around?"

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:29.000
And he was like...
[As Michaels] "Hmm.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.801
Do I want to stick around
to watch improv?

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:34.567
Uh, over my dead body?"

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.334
-Yeah, no.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.267
And -- Yeah, but anyways,
you end up being --

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:41.467
and working together and became
the Kids in the Hall.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.334
Mark, I don't know if you
remember this years ago

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:44.868
I met you.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.901
-Yes. 1996. That's right.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.567
I was on "Saturday Night Live."

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:51.367
Someone asked me to do a student
film in Troy, New York,

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:53.734
in the middle of winter,
so, naturally, I said yes.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:57.334
And I went up there, and there
was a sound guy doing the boom

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:58.767
who had a lot of energy.

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:01.033
Like, way, way too much energy.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.634
And that was...Jimmy Fallon.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:05.167
-I was excited, yeah.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.634
-Oh, you were...

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:09.734
Boom's in the shot!
"I'm on it! I'm on it!"

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.567
-"Should I be in the shot,
as well?!"

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.868
-"Can I -- Can I get in?!
Is the camera...?"

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.300
-I remember I was laying

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.767
under a coffee table
for one scene or whatever,

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:20.400
and I was holding a microphone,
and you were doing a scene.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.968
And I go, "Hey, Mark."
And you're like...

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.701
Doing your scene. You're like...

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.300
And I go...
-"Not now!"

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.033
-"I really want to be
on 'Saturday Night Live.'"

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:31.434
And you go, "Good luck, man.
It's going to be great."

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:34.067
-No, but we stayed in touch.
And then you sent -- By the way,

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.801
the sound on that film,
not great.

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.501
-I thought
that would be perfect.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.968
-No, but then later,
you sent me a VHS tape

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.367
and a really sweet letter
and said

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:43.767
could I pass it along
to someone.

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:45.868
-Yeah, I appreciate that.
You were great to me.

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:47.400
You were really nice.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.567
Why -- Why bring it back now?
Why -- Is it just demand?

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:52.801
Everyone wants to see
the Kids in the Hall now?

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.501
-Well, my astrologer told me

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.467
that one of us
was going to die soon.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:59.901
-Oh. Wow.
-And I'm the weak one, so...

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.934
-I actually paid his astrologer
to say that.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:06.534
-To say that --
-It was worth it.

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.133
It was worth it.
-This is a --

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:11.968
This is a photo I have from
season five here.

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:14.367
This is -- You guys were
all buried together.

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:15.767
-Yeah.
-Can we see this one? Yeah.

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:19.167
It was very funny.
It's not shocking. It's funny.

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:21.801
-It's funny.
-Here's what's good, is --

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:26.300
Season six, you guys
are back from the dead.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.934
In the exact same outfits.
The exact same positions.

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:30.200
It's so rad.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:34.367
-Thank you.

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:36.200
-Well, I can assume at this
point there's going to be --

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.601
There's going to be even more
"Kids in the Hall."

00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:40.934
Are you working
on a seventh season?

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.667
-Uh, we're told
it really all depends

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:44.267
how well this interview goes.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:47.167
-Yeah, so, in a word --
in a word, no.

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:50.067
-No? Yeah.
I cannot wait for this.

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:52.334
I'm so excited.
This Friday on Amazon Prime.

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:53.701
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:55.334
Here's a peek at the new season
of "Kids in the Hall."

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:56.701
Take a look.

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:58.300
-You ready to meet the fellas?

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.400
♪♪

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.834
=♪ We're fast, we're loose,
we're out of control ♪

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:10.100
♪ We're 60 years young
and on the pole ♪

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.801
[ Women screaming ]

00:07:12.801 --> 00:07:15.133
-Oh, my God! It is so, so sexy.

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:17.501
And there's a real sense
of danger. Mostly for them.

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.501
Because they could
really get hurt.

00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:22.567
-[ Women screaming ]
-Here he comes, ladies.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:26.133
Look at the love
and his reading glasses.

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:28.367
♪♪

00:07:28.367 --> 00:07:31.400
-I've been doing this since
they closed the Oshawa plant.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.634
Autoworkers and strippers
are in the same union,

00:07:34.634 --> 00:07:38.701
so, you know,
I got to keep my benefits.

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.801
-Oh, my God!
He still has a land line!

00:07:40.801 --> 00:07:43.267
That's so hot.

00:07:43.267 --> 00:07:45.200
[ Busy signal beeping ]

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.100
-"The Kids in the Hall,"
everybody.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.501
-Not bad.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.801
--The new season comes
to Prime Video this Friday.

